1
00:00:09,384 --> 00:00:10,636
This is ruined.

2
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:13,013
<i>I'm doomed.</i>

3
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:14,556
It's all messed up.

4
00:00:15,432 --> 00:00:17,684
<i>I have no hope.</i>

5
00:00:17,768 --> 00:00:19,186
Gosh.

6
00:00:19,478 --> 00:00:21,563
What are we going to do about this?

7
00:00:21,647 --> 00:00:23,982
<i>What am I going to do now?</i>

8
00:00:25,651 --> 00:00:26,902
Gong Yeon-su.

9
00:00:29,947 --> 00:00:33,825
I worked hard on it
but it didn't ferment.

10
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:38,539
- Gosh. Too bitter.
- What now?

11
00:00:38,622 --> 00:00:40,457
- What do you mean?
- Over one mistake...

12
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:44,002
Just because
it's not fermented properly

13
00:00:44,086 --> 00:00:45,462
are you throwing all this out?

14
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:48,549
I wish I could save it too.

15
00:00:49,007 --> 00:00:50,384
Do you know
how much these beans cost?

16
00:00:52,261 --> 00:00:54,388
How can I be saved

17
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:56,306
when not even <i>cheonggukjang</i>
can be saved?

18
00:00:58,517 --> 00:00:59,726
Find someone else

19
00:00:59,977 --> 00:01:01,853
who has a good understanding
of our company.

20
00:01:03,105 --> 00:01:05,315
I almost threw this at you.

21
00:01:05,399 --> 00:01:06,650
She was my blind date.

22
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:09,111
So what? Since when did you care
about your blind date?

23
00:01:09,194 --> 00:01:10,862
She threw up on my clothes
in the club.

24
00:01:10,946 --> 00:01:12,698
People make mistakes.

25
00:01:12,781 --> 00:01:14,032
<i>It's actually better this way.</i>

26
00:01:14,116 --> 00:01:15,909
It was
rather a sophisticated meeting.

27
00:01:16,451 --> 00:01:18,078
- Sophisticated?
- Yes.

28
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:22,040
They're mine. Perfect. I love it.

29
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:27,337
Drink.

30
00:01:33,176 --> 00:01:34,511
This isn't right.

31
00:01:34,595 --> 00:01:36,263
I'm sorry, Se-ra. I can't do it.

32
00:01:36,346 --> 00:01:39,016
You can't back out now.
You said you'd give it a shot.

33
00:01:39,099 --> 00:01:40,559
You had your hand up.

34
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:43,395
You don't think
I'm the right person for it either.

35
00:01:43,478 --> 00:01:44,479
I didn't.

36
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:47,482
But the tables have turned.

37
00:01:49,443 --> 00:01:51,695
- What do you mean?
- He was looking for you.

38
00:01:53,363 --> 00:01:54,573
The horizon.

39
00:01:54,656 --> 00:01:57,200
You went on and on and on
about the horizon.

40
00:01:57,284 --> 00:02:00,078
Now that I finally found the person,
what changed your mind?

41
00:02:00,162 --> 00:02:02,581
I'm not talking about the company.
Let's just change the marketer.

42
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,207
- What?
- Instead of that woman

43
00:02:04,291 --> 00:02:06,877
bring me the person
who came up with the horizon ad.

44
00:02:10,047 --> 00:02:11,506
Didn't I tell you?

45
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:12,799
She's the one.

46
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:16,386
- What?
- So, be confident.

47
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:19,431
You're not Gong Yeon-su
from the blind date

48
00:02:19,514 --> 00:02:21,308
but Gong Yeon-su
who created the horizon ad.

49
00:02:24,770 --> 00:02:27,397
Grapes for you.

50
00:02:27,689 --> 00:02:29,274
Mang-na. I knew I could count on you.

51
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:33,111
Hey, don't you think calling me
by my name

52
00:02:33,195 --> 00:02:34,988
when I'm 24 years older than you
is a bit much?

53
00:02:35,072 --> 00:02:36,365
I don't mind hearing it though.

54
00:02:36,448 --> 00:02:39,117
I do it to any women
who are older than me.

55
00:02:39,201 --> 00:02:41,328
I call every woman by their names
except for my mom.

56
00:02:42,663 --> 00:02:44,581
You're really not prejudiced.

57
00:02:44,665 --> 00:02:47,584
You're the reason I come to work,
to have fun with you.

58
00:02:51,463 --> 00:02:54,216
Excuse me.

59
00:03:13,694 --> 00:03:16,363
I'm sorry about last time.

60
00:03:16,446 --> 00:03:19,950
I don't normally drink that much.
But that day...

61
00:03:21,993 --> 00:03:24,287
Anyway, I'm sorry about that.

62
00:03:24,371 --> 00:03:27,791
- It's okay.
- And I'll pay you back

63
00:03:27,874 --> 00:03:31,920
- for your clothes.
- Sure.

64
00:03:51,231 --> 00:03:54,401
Has it been decided that you'll be
in charge of our product?

65
00:03:54,484 --> 00:03:57,404
- Yes, for now.
- Let me ask a few questions.

66
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:59,239
Have you ever used a sex toy before?

67
00:03:59,322 --> 00:04:01,950
- No.
- Including our products?

68
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:05,078
No, never.

69
00:04:05,162 --> 00:04:08,832
I didn't even know the name
of your company until I received it.

70
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:12,169
Is that a problem?

71
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:14,880
Which part?
Not knowing the name of our company?

72
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:16,798
Or no sex toy experience?

73
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:19,134
Being your blind date.

74
00:04:19,217 --> 00:04:22,345
- If that's what bugs you...
- Yes.

75
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:24,514
It bugs me.

76
00:04:24,598 --> 00:04:26,266
You being my blind date also bugs me.

77
00:04:26,349 --> 00:04:28,143
You've never used a sex toy before.

78
00:04:28,226 --> 00:04:30,228
And you didn't even know
the name of our company.

79
00:04:31,146 --> 00:04:33,023
Just because I didn't know the name

80
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:35,317
it doesn't mean I didn't know
what this company does.

81
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,569
Whether it's for a company
or a product or an event

82
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:39,571
the idea of marketing is the same.

83
00:04:39,738 --> 00:04:42,783
And it's my job to analyze and grasp

84
00:04:42,866 --> 00:04:44,659
- the target.
- Is that so?

85
00:04:45,827 --> 00:04:47,579
Since you said so,
let me ask you one more question.

86
00:04:49,414 --> 00:04:51,500
What do you think of sex toys?

87
00:04:54,753 --> 00:04:56,546
Do you have any intention
of using them in the future?

88
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:02,385
That answers my question.

89
00:05:02,469 --> 00:05:05,514
I can't leave it to a marketer
who's biased about our product.

90
00:05:06,473 --> 00:05:08,058
I think we're done here.

91
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:09,935
We're done here?

92
00:05:10,018 --> 00:05:11,436
Yes, we're done.

93
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:13,313
You need to leave.

94
00:05:37,629 --> 00:05:41,424
Yes, I admit
that I'm biased about your product.

95
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:43,301
I don't know much about it

96
00:05:43,385 --> 00:05:45,554
and I never really paid
attention to it.

97
00:05:46,096 --> 00:05:49,140
Honestly, it's true that I feel
a bit resistant to it in some ways.

98
00:05:49,224 --> 00:05:50,350
But you know what?

99
00:05:50,517 --> 00:05:55,480
You'll find a lot of people like me
in general.

100
00:05:55,564 --> 00:05:59,192
And they're your target in the end.

101
00:06:00,652 --> 00:06:05,907
Because I'm biased,
I know how to overcome that bias.

102
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:12,831
What does the horizon

103
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:14,457
mean to you?

104
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:17,335
The horizon ad.

105
00:06:18,336 --> 00:06:19,462
I heard it was your idea.

106
00:06:21,006 --> 00:06:22,465
I'm just curious
about what that means.

107
00:06:22,883 --> 00:06:24,134
Well, it's just...

108
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:26,845
a peaceful, safe

109
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:29,389
- and stable life.
- In detail.

110
00:06:32,309 --> 00:06:36,021
It's the line I keep my eyes on

111
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:39,816
so I don't lose where I'm going.

112
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:42,235
Sometimes I stop and look back to see

113
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:48,783
if I've strayed
from the path I wanted to take.

114
00:06:49,576 --> 00:06:50,744
It's the line

115
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:53,622
that makes me start walking again.

116
00:06:53,872 --> 00:06:55,081
You mean like

117
00:06:55,916 --> 00:06:58,585
marriage?

118
00:07:02,964 --> 00:07:07,052
Well, I'm not sure
whether it's a marriage or not.

119
00:07:07,552 --> 00:07:09,971
Because you can't guess
how far the horizon is.

120
00:07:10,347 --> 00:07:14,893
I'm still walking toward it,
but I haven't reached it yet.

121
00:07:16,519 --> 00:07:17,896
Does that answer your question?

122
00:07:21,232 --> 00:07:26,154
MAKE ME TINGLE

123
00:07:32,619 --> 00:07:34,621
Aunt Mi-young, it's not funny.

124
00:07:34,704 --> 00:07:36,247
No, I'm not saying it's funny.

125
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:39,000
I'm proud of you.

126
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:42,837
I knew people in this family

127
00:07:42,921 --> 00:07:46,257
tend to act first and think later.
It runs in the family.

128
00:07:46,341 --> 00:07:49,719
I'm about to go crazy
trying to do something crazy.

129
00:07:51,888 --> 00:07:53,890
What if I stray from the path

130
00:07:54,265 --> 00:07:56,601
- while trying a new one?
- What's wrong with it?

131
00:07:57,227 --> 00:07:58,728
Just because you know it,
doesn't mean you won't fall.

132
00:08:00,438 --> 00:08:03,483
Hey, life is no big deal.
Don't think too much about it.

133
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:06,194
Hey, it's burning. Flip it.

134
00:08:06,277 --> 00:08:07,821
- Flip it.
- It's not burned.

135
00:08:07,904 --> 00:08:09,155
It is.

136
00:08:30,802 --> 00:08:34,514
<i>It's the line I keep my eyes on</i>

137
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:37,934
<i>so I don't lose where I'm going.</i>

138
00:08:38,935 --> 00:08:43,648
<i>I'm still walking toward it,</i>
<i>but I haven't reached it yet.</i>

139
00:09:02,292 --> 00:09:04,335
<i>We finally have...</i>

140
00:09:04,419 --> 00:09:06,254
A new girl.

141
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:19,684
The vice president is late.

142
00:09:20,769 --> 00:09:23,772
Sorry. It was hard to put
on the butt-lifting shapewear today.

143
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:30,195
<i>His boyfriend?</i>

144
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:32,697
Say hi. He's our vice president.

145
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:35,575
Gong Yeon-su, right? I'm Yun Ji-o.

146
00:09:35,658 --> 00:09:37,911
Oh, yes. Hello.

147
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:40,580
This is Ma Mang-na,
the product designer.

148
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:42,332
He's Joo Min-hyung, the web designer.

149
00:09:42,499 --> 00:09:43,666
Nice to meet you.

150
00:09:44,626 --> 00:09:47,504
Finally, I'm not
the only woman here anymore.

151
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:50,799
Can I call you by your name
when the bosses aren't here?

152
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:53,843
I'm Gong Yeon-su
from SR Marketing Group.

153
00:09:53,927 --> 00:09:55,929
I'll be in charge
of promoting your new release.

154
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:59,599
I look forward to working with you.

155
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:01,267
You can call me

156
00:10:01,476 --> 00:10:03,895
Ms. Gong.

157
00:10:04,521 --> 00:10:07,273
The vice president will tell you
about the rest.

158
00:10:07,398 --> 00:10:09,109
- Sure.
- You're dismissed.

159
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:11,152
Oh, Mr. Dokgo.
You need to look at this.

160
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:13,488
This too.

161
00:10:15,281 --> 00:10:16,658
Here.

162
00:10:16,991 --> 00:10:19,119
- Is this my desk?
- Now

163
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:20,787
do you want me to show you around?

164
00:10:23,748 --> 00:10:26,376
You said you'd show me around.

165
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:28,795
Yes, it's the in-company cafe.

166
00:10:29,295 --> 00:10:30,964
This place has good coffee.

167
00:10:38,805 --> 00:10:40,598
Dal told me.

168
00:10:40,682 --> 00:10:42,350
You met on a blind date?

169
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:45,562
Don't take it wrong.

170
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:48,106
The blind date has nothing to do
with this...

171
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:51,276
I know. Dal seeing a woman
on a blind date

172
00:10:51,359 --> 00:10:52,944
of all people?

173
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:57,240
My boss is actually
pretty blunt and prickly.

174
00:10:57,490 --> 00:11:00,493
Still, he means no harm.
So don't take it personally.

175
00:11:00,577 --> 00:11:01,828
That's what I wanted to tell you.

176
00:11:02,537 --> 00:11:04,330
Yes, I'll do my best.

177
00:11:05,081 --> 00:11:07,542
Doing my best is my specialty.

178
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:10,587
Still

179
00:11:10,753 --> 00:11:13,464
I'm new to this field.

180
00:11:13,631 --> 00:11:15,508
I'm going to need your help.

181
00:11:15,592 --> 00:11:16,885
Of course.

182
00:11:16,968 --> 00:11:18,469
Feel free to ask me.

183
00:11:18,553 --> 00:11:19,804
I'll be here to help you.

184
00:11:20,638 --> 00:11:23,391
But don't tell Dal.

185
00:11:23,474 --> 00:11:26,060
Does it have to be a secret?

186
00:11:26,144 --> 00:11:27,645
He won't say anything good anyway.

187
00:11:27,729 --> 00:11:29,564
From what I know...

188
00:11:30,732 --> 00:11:33,109
Mind your own business.

189
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:40,366
You guys look pretty close.

190
00:11:41,618 --> 00:11:43,536
Whatever. I hate you.

191
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:45,622
Honey, don't be upset.

192
00:11:49,334 --> 00:11:51,044
Still...

193
00:11:51,127 --> 00:11:53,713
Now, let's talk about the tuition.

194
00:11:53,796 --> 00:11:55,465
- The tuition?
- I'm not asking for much.

195
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:57,717
A cup of coffee
from time to time will do.

196
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:00,678
Well, sure.

197
00:12:00,762 --> 00:12:03,473
Oh, right. That means you need money.

198
00:12:05,016 --> 00:12:06,976
- Ta-da.
- My wallet.

199
00:12:07,268 --> 00:12:08,686
- How do you have this?
- Well...

200
00:12:09,479 --> 00:12:11,064
I found it in front of the club.

201
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:12,857
Oh, thank you so much.

202
00:12:13,191 --> 00:12:15,902
I reported everything lost.

203
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:17,570
You owe me one.

204
00:12:17,779 --> 00:12:20,365
- Now, are you ready for a real tour?
- Yes.

205
00:12:28,915 --> 00:12:31,584
This is where we try the products.

206
00:12:31,668 --> 00:12:32,752
What?

207
00:12:33,294 --> 00:12:34,712
In the company?

208
00:12:34,796 --> 00:12:37,131
- Yes. Something wrong?
- But...

209
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:41,052
- During work?
- It is work.

210
00:12:41,135 --> 00:12:42,303
It's part of our job.

211
00:12:44,055 --> 00:12:46,474
You're free to use it anytime.

212
00:12:46,808 --> 00:12:48,351
Oh, don't forget to lock the door.

213
00:12:48,935 --> 00:12:52,063
No, I'm good.

214
00:12:56,276 --> 00:12:58,653
- Are you using it?
- No.

215
00:13:01,072 --> 00:13:02,949
This is the Development Room

216
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:04,909
where we design
and engineer everything.

217
00:13:05,618 --> 00:13:07,704
After the prototypes are made
at the factory

218
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:09,580
we test and improve them here.

219
00:13:09,664 --> 00:13:12,959
This is where you can see
the entire history of Loand.

220
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:23,344
All right. Here's a test.

221
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:28,099
- Guess what this is.
- Is that also a toy?

222
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:30,018
It looks like a tumbler, doesn't it?

223
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:34,772
We have ones that look
like eggs and muffins.

224
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:38,693
Our ancestors used
animals' horns or wood.

225
00:13:38,776 --> 00:13:42,572
Guess when the oldest sex toy
in human history was made.

226
00:13:44,574 --> 00:13:47,577
- I'm not sure.
- It was 30,000 years ago.

227
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:50,455
This world has history too.

228
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:51,956
Of course.

229
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:55,251
Cleopatra

230
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:57,628
put a bunch of bees inside a gourd

231
00:13:57,712 --> 00:13:59,380
and made it vibrate artificially.

232
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:02,050
Cleopatra. Wow.

233
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:15,229
- And here's your homework.
- For me?

234
00:14:18,149 --> 00:14:20,026
What is this?

235
00:14:20,109 --> 00:14:23,780
Think about why
mankind created things like this.

236
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,198
Think about it?

237
00:14:27,158 --> 00:14:28,201
Okay.

238
00:15:07,865 --> 00:15:10,493
Be good. Stay quiet.

239
00:15:16,999 --> 00:15:20,503
<i>Yusecha</i>

240
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:26,092
<i>Eolsachirwol gapjasang</i>

241
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:29,178
So? Is your crazy thing worth doing?

242
00:15:30,555 --> 00:15:32,181
I'm getting used to it.

243
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:34,600
By any chance

244
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:37,645
are you bringing any toys home?

245
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,481
Are you crazy?

246
00:15:43,443 --> 00:15:44,944
How can I bring them home?

247
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:46,529
Hey. You brought coffee home
all the time

248
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:48,948
when you were working
on the coffee ad.

249
00:15:49,574 --> 00:15:50,783
Hush.

250
00:15:53,202 --> 00:15:56,456
<i>Chuwongamsi</i>

251
00:15:56,706 --> 00:16:00,001
<i>Bulseongyeongmo</i>

252
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:03,004
<i>Geuni</i>

253
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:06,007
<i>Jeongjakseosu</i>

254
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:07,550
It's not me.

255
00:16:10,887 --> 00:16:12,680
Seriously, Nam-su...

256
00:16:21,439 --> 00:16:23,274
Wait!

257
00:16:24,317 --> 00:16:25,693
What's going on?

258
00:16:25,776 --> 00:16:28,321
- What's wrong?
- Uncle.

259
00:16:28,529 --> 00:16:29,780
